************************************************************************ CtlPatch.ASM** * Copyright 1988* Apple Computer, Inc.* All rights Reserved.** This file contains a jump table and jumps back into the regular code.* It is designed so that it can be linked to the version of the control* manager that is a single file in RAM and not to be used when it is* in ROM.** A different version of this table is used in ROM so that more than* one tool can use it.*** Change History** 11 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Coding begins.****************************************************************************************************************************************ToolboxPatcher	PROC EXPORT** This is the only entry point to this code.  The control* manager calls to this routine with the x-register set* to indicate what real call it wants to make.** In this way, the call can be patched.*** Inputs:*	x-reg    Call To Make** Outputs:*	no registers are altered.** External Refs:*	The real routines.** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	jmp (Table,x)Table	dc.w ToCMDispatcher	dc.w oopsToCMDispatcher		import RealCMDispatcher	jml RealCMDispatcherOops	brk 17	ENDP	END